## GET /api/politics/fec/contributions

The company-politics contribution feed. With `aggregated=true` (the default) rows are at the
company × candidate × cycle × tier grain - filter by `ticker` for a company's candidates, or by
`candidate_id` for a candidate's companies. With `aggregated=false` rows are individual
contributions, paginated by `cursor` (pass back `next_cursor` from the previous response);
`tier` selects `pac` (default) or `employee`.

This is an enterprise only endpoint. Contact dev@unusualwhales.com for details about accessing this data.


```json
[
  {
    "description": "Default true.",
    "in": "query",
    "name": "aggregated",
    "required": false,
    "schema": {
      "type": "boolean"
    }
  },
  {
    "description": "",
    "in": "query",
    "name": "candidate_id",
    "required": false,
    "schema": {
      "type": "integer"
    }
  },
  {
    "description": "Row-level only, ISO date.",
    "in": "query",
    "name": "min_date",
    "required": false,
    "schema": {
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  {
    "description": "Row-level only, ISO date.",
    "in": "query",
    "name": "max_date",
    "required": false,
    "schema": {
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  {
    "description": "Row-level keyset cursor.",
    "in": "query",
    "name": "cursor",
    "required": false,
    "schema": {
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  {
    "description": "Page number (default 1).",
    "in": "query",
    "name": "page",
    "required": false,
    "schema": {
      "type": "integer"
    }
  },
  {
    "description": "Rows per page (default 50, max 200).",
    "in": "query",
    "name": "limit",
    "required": false,
    "schema": {
      "type": "integer"
    }
  }
]

```

